Q:
(b) The equation F = 9/5 C + 32 gives the relationship between temperature in degrees Fahrenheit (F) and temperature in degrees celsius (C).

1. What is the slope of the graph describing the relationship between F and C?

2. What is the (average) rate of change of the temperature in degrees Fahrenheit with respect to the temperature in degrees Celsius?

3. What is the net change in the temperature in degrees Fahrenheit when the temperature in degrees Celsius increases by 1?

A:
1. m = 9/5

2. AROC = Delta F / Delta C = 9/5

3. Delta F = 9/5 when Delta C = 1

KEYWORDS: slope, rate of change
